        <body>
            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0543" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.124/201.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 97.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, referring to my despatch
                    No. 77 of March 23, 1912, to report that on April 6 the enclosed memorandum in
                    regard to the sanitation of Guayaquil was received from the Ecuadorian Foreign
                    Office.</p>
                <p>It has been suggested to me verbally by the Minister for Foreign Affairs that
                    immediately upon the expiration of the Coignet contract the proper staff of
                    medical officers and engineers be sent to Guayaquil by the Panama Canal
                    Commission to conduct the survey.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rutherfurd Bingham</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d629-a1.xml" xpointer="d629-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
